  <h1>Cloud Computing Career Guide 2026: Skills, Courses and Job Opportunities</h1>

  <p>
    Cloud computing has become an important part of modern IT
    infrastructure. Businesses use cloud platforms to store data,
    run applications, manage resources and support digital services.
    Students interested in technology can explore cloud computing
    as a potential career path.
  </p>

  <h2>What Is Cloud Computing?</h2>

  <p>
    Cloud computing provides computing resources such as servers,
    storage, databases and networking over the internet. It helps
    organizations access technology resources without maintaining
    every physical server themselves.
  </p>

  <h2>Popular Cloud Computing Platforms</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Amazon Web Services (AWS)</li>
    <li>Microsoft Azure</li>
    <li>Google Cloud Platform (GCP)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Important Skills to Learn</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Computer Networking Fundamentals</li>
    <li>Linux Administration</li>
    <li>Windows Server Fundamentals</li>
    <li>Cloud Computing Fundamentals</li>
    <li>Python or PowerShell Basics</li>
    <li>Identity and Access Management</li>
    <li>Cloud Security Fundamentals</li>
    <li>Monitoring and Troubleshooting</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cloud Computing Career Opportunities</h2>

  <p>
    Depending on their knowledge, practical skills and experience,
    learners may work towards roles such as:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Cloud Support Associate</li>
    <li>Cloud Support Engineer</li>
    <li>Junior Systems Administrator</li>
    <li>Cloud Engineer</li>
    <li>Cloud Security Analyst</li>
    <li>DevOps Engineer</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Advanced positions generally require relevant professional
    experience and deeper technical knowledge.
  </p>

  <h2>How Can Beginners Start Learning Cloud Computing?</h2>

  <ol>
    <li>Learn computer hardware and operating system basics.</li>
    <li>Understand IP addressing, DNS and networking.</li>
    <li>Practise Linux commands and server administration.</li>
    <li>Choose a cloud platform and learn its core services.</li>
    <li>Build practical projects in a cloud lab.</li>
    <li>Explore relevant certifications and entry-level roles.</li>
  </ol>

